  "body": "[A10] Correction to the #185/#186 assignment, item 2. I wrote that the lock-timeout notification (Milan v1.2 Table 5.22) keeps flags 0. That came from me, not from a clause, and it is withdrawn.\n\nMilan v1.2 Table 5.22 says only that the notification is sent when the entity automatically unlocks itself after one minute; it does not define the flags. Where Milan is silent, IEEE 1722.1-2021 decides. Its 7.5.2 sends a notification as an unsolicited response, and an unlock response carries UNLOCK (7.4.2.1, Table 7-143). The in-house qualification expects UNLOCK as well, and found the automatic-unlock notification carrying flags 0.\n\nSo both unlock notifications, the command-driven one and the automatic one after the timeout, carry flags UNLOCK with locked_id 0. If the lane's round-1 head keeps flags 0 for the timeout case, the change goes into round 2.",
